# Outage Crawler — Project Rules

## Stack

- Next.js
- TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS
- Supabase PostgreSQL
- Vercel
- Hourly scraper

## General

- Use TypeScript.
- Follow existing patterns before introducing new ones.
- Do not create duplicate components or utilities.
- Prefer simple solutions over unnecessary abstractions.
- Do not modify unrelated files.
- Preserve existing functionality when making changes.

## UI Consistency

- Reuse existing components.
- Follow DESIGN.md.
- Do not introduce new colors, typography, spacing systems, or components without checking existing patterns.
- Maintain responsive behavior.
- Keep the interface clean and information-focused.

## Database

- Supabase is the source of truth.
- Every outage must have a source URL.
- Prevent duplicate advisories.
- Use proper foreign keys.
- Never expose service-role credentials to the client.

## Scraper

- Scraper runs once per hour.
- Scraping must be idempotent.
- Never delete existing outage records merely because an advisory is temporarily unavailable.
- Store the original source URL.
- Log parsing failures.
- Parser changes must not break previously parsed formats.

## Before coding

1. Inspect existing implementation.
2. Identify reusable components/functions.
3. Check relevant documentation.
4. Make the smallest appropriate change.
5. Run lint/type checks.
6. Test the affected functionality.